/TU (Page 2 of 14\056 Privacy Act Statement\015Collection and Use of Personal Information\056 Sections 205\050ay\051\054 223\050d\051\054 1614\050ay\051\054 and 1631 of the Social Security Act\054 as amended\054 allow us to collect this information\056  Furnishing us this information is voluntary\056  However\054 failing to provide all or part of the information may prevent an accurate and timely decision on any claim filed\056 We will use the information to make a determination on eligibility for benefits\056  We may also share your information for the following purposes\054 called routine uses\072 \200 To contractors and other Federal agencies\054 as necessary\054 for the purpose of assisting the Social Security Administration \050SSA\051 in the efficient administration of its programs\073 and \200 To applicants\054 claimants\054 prospective applicants or claimants\054 other than the data subject\054 their authorized representatives or representative payees to the extent necessary to pursue Social Security claims and to representative payees when the information pertains to individuals for whom they serve as representative payees\054 for the purpose of assisting SSA in administering its representative payment responsibilities under the Act and assisting the representative payees in performing their duties as payees\054 including receiving and accounting for benefits for individuals for whom they serve as payees\056 In addition\054 we may share this information in accordance with the Privacy Act and other Federal laws\056  For example\054 where authorized\054 we may use and disclose this information in computer matching programs\054 in which our records are compared with other records to establish or verify a person\047s eligibility for Federal benefit programs and for repayment of incorrect or delinquent debts under these programs\056 Ay list of additional routine uses is available in our Privacy Act System of Records Notices \050S O R N\051 60\0550089\054 entitled Claims Folders System\054 as published in the Federal Register \050F R\051 on April 1\054 2003\054 at 68 F R 15784\054 and 60\0550320\054 entitled Electronic Disability Claim File\054 as published in the F R on December 22\054 2003\054 at 68 F R 71210\056  Additional information\054 and a full listing of all of our S O R Ns\054 is available on our website at w w w\056s s ay\056g o v\057privacy\056 )
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
